    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{15}{4}=3\\dfrac{3}{4}$, which is $\\dfrac14$ from $4$. Choose 15 as the numerator and 4 as the denominator.",
      "worked": "Choose 15 as the numerator and 4 as the denominator.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{15}{4}&=3\\frac34\\\\4-3\\frac34&=\\frac14\\end{align*}$$\nWith denominator 3, the closest choice is $\\frac{10}{3}=3\\frac13$, which is $\\frac23$ from 4. The other choice above 4 is $\\frac{15}{3}=5$, which is 1 from 4. Every remaining fraction is at most 3, so $\\frac{15}{4}$ is closest.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
